    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d333">

                <pb facs="0544" n="458" xml:id="pg458"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">863.51 Relief Credits/6: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Austria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Washburn</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-12-02T11:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 2,
                                1927—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 2—10:02
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>66. Enclosure 1 to my despatch 1573, October 17. Austrian Government abandons its
                    request for extension until 1957 of time of payment of principal and interest,
                    leaving only its request that assets pledged for payment of the United States
                    Grain Corporation Loan may be subordinated to contemplated new Federal loan. See
                    joint resolution of Congress April 6th, 1922, transmitted with my despatch No.
                    1037, May 10, 1926.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d333-f1"/> Explanatory despatch 1629
                    mailed 30th ultimo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washburn</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
